Unexported dmsynth sink startup/lifetime hardening, recovered 2026-08-19.

Found in ../recovered-session/wine-11.0/dlls/dmsynth/synthsink.c with an
mtime of 2026-08-17 23:24, i.e. after the 18:26 build of the production
dmsynth_p34_interp_reset.dll and before the 23:34 build of
dmsynth_audit_round3.dll.  It is present in the audit_round3 binary, absent
from production p34, and was never exported into wine-patches/.

It propagates each sink thread's startup HRESULT back to synth_sink_activate,
closes the thread handles, resets the stop events on every failure and on
deactivate, and frees the render buffer on the early-failure paths.  None of it
has been measured on the device, and it is NOT part of dmsynth p35: the p35
watchdog was built on the production p34 source recovered from the patch chain,
so the two changes stay separable.

Applies on top of the NO-ISLAND chain with `patch -p1 -F0` as long as patch 60
is not applied.  The two are not stackable as they stand: this diff and patch 60
both rewrite the `if (!started)` startup-signal region of the timing thread, so
the last hunk of whichever is applied second has to be merged by hand.

Kept here so the tree revert does not lose it.

